# Runtime state written by the guard and its host hook — never committed
server/keep-alive.lock
server/keep-alive.out


# Evidence packs are staged with `git add -f` (see the pack READMEs, and pack-check.py, which FAILS
# when a pack file is untracked). Until 2026-10-22 a negation here un-ignored every evidence log so a
# pack's own log could not be dropped silently - but that is exactly what let `git add -A` sweep
# ANOTHER member's live log into an unrelated commit (measured 2026-10-21; it cost a force-push).
# gitignore cannot tell a filed pack log from one still being written, so evidence logs are ignored
# like every other log and force-added deliberately. The original defect (a pack that CITES a log it
# never committed) is caught by pack-check.py and by reading the staged list both ways.
